visa\nATAS clearance\nWorking in the UK\nWorking in the UK\nAfter graduation\nSpend part of your degree here\nSpend part of your degree here\nInternational and European exchange\nFee-paying study abroad\nVisiting postgraduate research students\nVisiting students modules\nEnglish language proficiency\nPreparing for Nottingham\nContact or meet us\nEvents in your country\nWhen applying to study at the University of Nottingham you must be able to evidence you have met the English Language requirements for your chosen course.\nThe requirements vary depending on course. Details can be found in our prospectus or as a condition of your offer letter. The University recognise a variety of qualifications to demonstrate your language ability.\nIf you don't have the required level of English\nAcademic English courses\nOur innovative courses help you improve your English and academic skills before you study with us.\nFind a course\nApplicants from English speaking countries\nIf you're a native English speaker, or you have studied in an English-speaking country or institution, we may be able to accept your academic qualifications as evidence of your English language ability. Check the list of approved countries on the UK government website.\nIf you haven't taken any qualifications meeting the criteria listed above, you will need to provide an English language test result, such as IELTS, PTE or TOEFL. See below for further guidance.\nSpeakers of other languages\nWe accept a variety of English language tests and qualifications. The International English Language Testing System (IELTS) Academic test is one of the most common. The IELTS test includes grades in listening, reading, writing and speaking, plus an overall grade. IELTS requirements for each of our courses are listed in our course listings.\nWe also accept Pearson Test of English (PTE) and TOEFL (IBT) test certificates (PTE Online is excluded), as well as a range of academic qualifications from various countries. Check our English language equivalencies information against the IELTS requirement listed in our course listings to see what grade you will need.\nYou can also meet our entry requirements through a presessional English course with our Centre for English Language Education (CELE).\nEnglish language entry policies\nMinimum English language entry requirements policy\nAlternative English language entry qualifications policy\nContact our student enquiry team for any queries about English language requirements\nQuick links\nApplicant help and support\nAcademic schools and departments\nProfessional services\nVisit our Sport page\nCripps Health Centre\nLakeside Arts\nFind out more about our conference facilities\nStudents\nStudent services\nHealth and wellbeing\nDigital services\nMoodle\nLibrary\nStaff\nWorking here\nWellbeing\nDigital services\nVacancies\nAlumni\nCommunity\nConnect with our alumni through news and events\nDonate\nGet in touch\n+44(0) 115 951 5151\nLines are open:\nMonday-Friday 9.00am-4.30pm\nUniversity of Nottingham\nUniversity Park\nNottingham, NG7 2RD\nUnited Kingdom\nQuick links\nApplicant help and support\nAcademic schools and departments\nProfessional services\nSport\nCripps Health Centre\nLakeside Arts\nConferences\nStudents\nStudent services\nHealth and wellbeing\nDigital services\nMoodle\nLibrary\nStaff\nWorking here\nWellbeing\nDigital services\nVacancies\nAlumni\nCommunity\nConnect\nDonate\nCopyright \u00a9 2010 - 2026 University of Nottingham\nPrivacy\n| Terms and conditions\n| Accessibility\n| Posting rules\n| Freedom of information\n| Charity gateway\n| Cookie policy |\nCookie Settings\n| Modern slavery statement", "links": [["", "https://www.nottingham.ac.uk/"], ["Study with us", "https://www.nottingham.ac.uk/studywithus/study-with-us.aspx"], ["Undergraduate", "https://www.nottingham.ac.uk/studywithus/ugstudy/find-uon.html"], ["Postgraduate", "https://www.nottingham.ac.uk/pgstudy/"], ["International students", "https://www.nottingham.ac.uk/studywithus/